# Paths where a change is dangerous in a way the diff does not show.
#
# This repository is public, so anyone may open a pull request from a fork.
# Nobody outside has write access and nothing outside has ever merged — the
# gate is review, and review is one person. This file is that person's
# tripwire: GitHub marks a pull request as touching an owned path, so a small
# diff in a security-bearing table cannot read as a routine change.
#
# It is not enforcement. With a single owner, CODEOWNERS cannot supply a
# second pair of eyes; it supplies a label that says "read this one properly".
# Treat a flagged pull request as one where the resolution path has to be
# walked by hand, not skimmed.

# Default: everything, so no path is silently unowned.
*                           @CtrlCarlitos

# The capability table. Each entry says what a plane's native tool *is* —
# Command, Mutation, SafeControl, Delegation, Deny. Change one entry and a tool
# stops being evaluated by the family that guards it, with no rule edited and
# nothing in the diff that looks like a policy change. The highest-leverage
# file in the repository for its size.
/internal/planecontract/    @CtrlCarlitos

# The rules themselves, and the tokenizer they read. A parse that shifts by one
# word changes every verdict keyed on it (#178).
/internal/engine/           @CtrlCarlitos

# The shipped floor: secret globs, safe roots, egress allowlist. A widened glob
# is a permission grant written as a config line.
/internal/policy/base.toml  @CtrlCarlitos

# Approval machinery: the broker, the named-pipe transport, WebAuthn
# enrolment, and the private-file ACL checks those depend on. This is what
# stands between an agent's request and an operator's consent.
/internal/approval/         @CtrlCarlitos
/internal/operatorauth/     @CtrlCarlitos
/internal/privatefs/        @CtrlCarlitos

# What the planes are told to run. genconfig emits the hook commands; a change
# here can leave a floor registered and unspawnable, which reads green
# everywhere else (#149).
/internal/genconfig/        @CtrlCarlitos

# CI decides whether any of the above is checked at all. The windows job in
# particular selects tests by name and package, so a Windows test can be made
# invisible by editing this file rather than the test (#163).
/.github/workflows/         @CtrlCarlitos
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @CtrlCarlitos
